title: write_secret and the other writes return undef on 404 instead of croaking
updated: 2026-10-15T03:13:30Z
---

`_request` maps every 404 to `undef` (`lib/WWW/OpenBao.pm:37`). For reads that is the documented soft miss. For writes it hides a failed operation: OpenBao answers 404 (`no handler for route`) when the KV mount does not exist or is KV v1, so with a mistyped `kv_mount`

    $bao->write_secret('app/db', { password => $pw });   # returns undef, no exception

stores nothing and raises nothing. The POD of `write_secret` (`lib/WWW/OpenBao.pm:285-288`) says only "Returns the decoded response"; a caller who does not test the return value loses the secret. The same holds for `enable_engine` (line 179), `unseal` (173), `init` (165), `destroy_secret`, `undelete_secret` and `soft_delete_secret` with versions.

k10 is the same defect for `login_k8s`; this card is the write side and can be fixed with it (same contract change, same consumers goldmine and hiplatform to warn).

Done: `_request` takes a flag (or the write methods check) so that a 404 on a write croaks with method, path and body like every other non-2xx; reads and `secret_exists` keep the soft miss; POD and README state it; a test per write method in `t/20-request.t`.

